# nr-tui-widgets-panels: wire lines for mixdog-tui-widgets (context inspector, context panel, usage panel, /btw panel)

No hot file needs a change. No protocol method, no service, nothing in compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING, no new workspace
dependency edge (the crate already depends on mixdog-js, mixdog-markdown-ansi, mixdog-term, mixdog-termtext, mixdog-tui-style
and mixdog-view-model; `mixdog_js::time` and `mixdog_js::math` are used, `chrono-tz` comes through it).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tui-widgets/tests/recorders/record-ink-frames.mjs (not a hot file, owned by nr-tui-widgets-base: the lead applies it)

The generic recorder bundles the components it names in `MODULES`; the corpus of this task (tests/cases/panels.json, written
by tests/recorders/gen-panels-cases.mjs) needs three more. In the `MODULES` object, after the `ConfirmBar` line add:

    ContextPanel: './ContextPanel.jsx',
    UsagePanel: './UsagePanel.jsx',
    BtwPanel: './BtwPanel.jsx',

(ContextInspector.jsx is bundled through ContextPanel.jsx.) tests/goldens/panels.json was recorded with exactly these three
lines added in a throw-away copy of the recorder (removed again); with them in place
`node tests/recorders/record-ink-frames.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --cases tests/cases/panels.json --check tests/goldens/panels.json`
passes. The recorder's spies return nothing, so a recorded `onInspect` settles as "Preview unavailable."; the replay in
tests/panels_twin.rs settles every fetch the same way. The preview text, the stale and the failed answers are covered by unit
tests in context_inspector.rs.

## What the application task (nr-tui-app, the /usage, /context and /btw controllers) must apply

The widgets are pure: props in, painted rows out, a state value for the keys.

* `panels::context_panel`: `ContextPanelProps` (rows, title, columns, fill_height, detail, description, panel_rows),
  `ContextPanelState` (call `sync(&props)` when the detail changes, then `handle_key(input, &key, &props)`, which returns an
  `InspectorEffect`: `Refresh` is `onRefresh`, `Inspect { id, revision, token }` is `onInspect(id, revision)`; give the answer
  to `finish_inspect(token, InspectOutcome::Answer(Option<Value>) | Failed)`; an answer of a preview that was left meanwhile is
  dropped by the token), `paint_context_panel`, `context_panel_rows`.
* `panels::usage_panel`: `UsagePanelProps` takes the clock reading `now_ms` (the reset time is written against it), keys go to
  `UsagePanelState::handle_key(&key, &props)`, `paint_usage_panel`, `usage_panel_rows`.
* `panels::btw_panel`: `BtwPanelProps`, `BtwPanelState::handle_key(&key, &props)`, `paint_btw_panel`, `btw_panel_rows`. The row
  arithmetic btw-controller.mjs exports and the panel imports is here (`BTW_CHROME_ROWS`, `btw_content_rows`, `btw_scroll_max`,
  `btw_scroll_offset`); the controller task keeps `btwPanelRows` (`BTW_CHROME_ROWS + min(10, btw_content_rows)`), the usage
  hint and the request sequence on top of them rather than porting them again.
* Each paint function returns the rows it took; each `*_rows` function gives the same count without painting.
